  "plan": {
    "goal": "Establish an endothelial-lined arterial microfluidic channel that recapitulates physiological arterial wall shear stress (~1 Pa) on HUVEC.",
    "rationale": "HUVEC physiological shear range is 0.1-1.0 Pa (registry, convention for microvascular/arterial endothelium). Arterial shear is at the upper end (~1 Pa). A 1000 µm × 100 µm × 20 mm PDMS channel at 100 µL/min delivers 1.0 Pa wall shear (verified via flow_rate_for_shear_stress and wall_shear_stress). Reynolds ≈ 3.0 (firmly laminar), pressure drop ≈ 400 Pa (~4 cm H2O, within syringe-pump range), residence time ≈ 1.2 s. HUVEC seeded at 15,000 cells/cm² (within 10,000-20,000 registry range) over 0.2 cm² culture area = 3000 cells. Medium viscosity assumed water-like (1e-3 Pa·s). O2 delivery at 100 µL/min is 0.02 µmol/min, ample for a small endothelial monolayer (HUVEC OCR not in registry; endothelial demand is low).",
