    "caveats": [
      "Confirm HUVEC OCR in-house; registry has no OCR for HUVEC, so O2 supply was checked only via delivery rate (0.02 µmol/min at 100 µL/min) — endothelial demand is low but should be confirmed.",
      "Verify the syringe pump can hold 100 µL/min against ~400 Pa backpressure (well within standard pump range).",
      "Coat the channel (e.g. fibronectin/collagen) before seeding to promote HUVEC adhesion and monolayer formation.",
      "Confirm the 1.0 Pa target is appropriate for the specific arterial context; arterial shear can range up to ~1.5 Pa in vivo.",
      "Check monolayer confluence and junctional markers (VE-cadherin) rather than TEER, which is low for HUVEC (~20-100 Ω·cm²) and not a reliable readout.",
      "Medium viscosity assumed 1e-3 Pa·s (water-like); if using a higher-viscosity medium, recalculate flow for the same shear."
    ]
